description "Hold dsp.A across follow-up plans for an interactive debug session."

# Cross-session device hold. Three-phase flow:
#
# 1. SUBMIT THIS PLAN. The token is delivered ONLY in the
#    artefact's manifest.json under "lease_token" -- never in
#    streams or timeline events, so a tunnel-side observer can't
#    read it from /inflight while the session is live. Read it:
#       python3 submit.py examples/lease_claim.plan \
#         --wait 5 --extract /tmp/lease
#       python3 -c 'import json,sys; \
#         print(json.load(open("/tmp/lease/manifest.json"))["lease_token"])'
#
# 2. ANY NUMBER OF RESUME PLANS while the lease is live (10 min by
#    default below). Use examples/lease_resume.plan as a template,
#    or write your own that starts with `lease:resume token="..."`.
#    Other agents trying to acquire dsp.A during the window get a
#    fast BusyError instead of grabbing it.
#
# 3. RELEASE WHEN DONE. examples/lease_release.plan or just let the
#    duration expire.

lease:claim devices="dsp.A" duration_s=600
